            "review_title": "Review at Shabu Ya",
            "review_text": "Jan F\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam56 contributions\n0\nnot vietnamese but really good buffet\nDec 2018\nWe eat at this type of buffet often, it's not Vietnamese, but their easy to find in shopping malls around town and it's fun to sit around with family and friends enjoying a meal. They give you a standard plate of noodles and vegetables and you order slice beef, pork, seafood plates to go in the soup, they also have a buffet table of noodles, veggies, a ground meat in a ceramic bamboo that is spicy like Mexican chorizo to put in the soup. Soda's and teas are self serve also ice cream. It's just a lot of fun, I have trouble with the shrimp as it isn't peeled and I can't eat it with the shell on like my Vietnamese family, but other than that I would recommend everything.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 15, 2019\nLeKienLki\nWe're pleased to know that your experience with us was good one, Jan. Thank you for taking a moment to recommend us to others. Your kind words are greatly appreciated and we hope you won't hesitate to let us know if we can serve you in the future.\nRead more\nWritten January 25, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
