            "review_title": "Review at Shabu Ya",
            "review_text": "Gin128\n17 contributions\n0\nYou can eat everything you like\nAug 2017 • Friends\nYou can choice 2 types of soup base (out of 5). My friends and I tried the Sukiyaki (made from Japanese soy sauce) and Miso (fermented soybean) with beef and shrimp. You can eat unlimited servings of the beef, pork, chicken and mini octopus. The beef was fresh.\nShabu Ya had the Healthy bar in the center of the restaurant. It was a large counter filled with endless amounts of broccoli, Udon, corn, beancurd skin, mushrooms ..etc. I really liked sausage. Especially, free sort drinks, ice cream and Japanese ice tea.\nIt was good value for money, about $7 per person (included VAT), for Happy Hour.\nFinally, Service was very attentive and young.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 22, 2017",
