            "review_title": "Review at Shabu Ya",
            "review_text": "p911turbo\nTexas474 contributions\n0\nNot a bad choice\nJul 2017 • Family\nThe food station was clean even though it does not have a lot of choices. The food was fresh and the broth was yummy. You can order beef, chicken, pork, octopus, shrimps. They provide only soda and so my daughter had to drink her own bottle of water. They have some desserts to choose from like jello, ice cream, local ban flan, etc.\n\nAgain, they have limited English and so I had a hard time understanding how it worked. When you go there, just make sure you take a look at the check carefully because they will automatically add 2000 dong for wet tissues even though we didn't use them. We paid about US$20 for lunch and we ate a lot of veggies.\nRead more\nWritten July 11, 2017",
